  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI28-ARCH-001" ;
  triage:title "runtime_health.rs RULE-003 threshold still exceeded (line count reduced but not resolved)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs line count is now 1271 lines, improved from the previous 1356 lines recorded in AI27-ARCH-001, but still exceeds the RULE-003 hard limit of 1250 lines. This finding carries forward the unresolved RULE-003 violation from the prior sprint. The component adds new health-check logic for peer recovery coordinator coordination, which contributes to the continued line-count pressure. While the absolute line count improved, the file remains out of compliance. Fix required: refactor runtime_health.rs to extract distinct responsibilities (e.g., peer recovery health checks, overall host health aggregation, external reporting) into separate modules to bring line count under 1250." ;
  triage:category "Architecture" ;
  triage:severity "Important" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T23:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Independently re-verified against real code on fix/ai28-phase-general-cleanup at commit 025bc6c7 (not accepted from arch-ctm's self-report). crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs is now 1183 lines (under the 1250 RULE-003 limit); doctor-report finalization/observability-finding logic extracted into crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/doctor_reporting.rs (92 lines), a genuine responsibility split with pub(super) visibility, not a mechanical relocation -- module is wired via mod doctor_reporting; and use doctor_reporting::{daemon_observability_finding, finalize_doctor_report}; at runtime_health.rs lines 34/45. ruthless-boundary-qa (scoped to this PR's touched files) returned PASS: narrowest-visibility pub(super) surface, no circular dependency back into runtime_health.rs internals, no duplicate implementation elsewhere in the workspace." ;
